 "conclusion": "every host function of the cuda delete and insert stages (the escher device store's erase, insert, v2h_remove, v2h_append, to_keys; group_by_vertex; the introsort) has the same instruction stream as the merge base's; only their alignments moved again (the device store's insert and to_keys from 32 to 16 mod 64, v2h_append from 16 to 0, group_by_vertex from 16 to 0, the introsort from 48 to 32), as the code the review added elsewhere in libdyng shifted them. The one changed function is still id_allocator::erase (host backends). Code placement, as step 5 located it; the device code is SASS-identical (M11a-sass-identity-0.3.json)."
